# The inventory's two outputs are generated from the repository by
# `node tools/inventory/main.mjs --write`. Two branches that both regenerate
# them conflict textually in a file nobody should hand-merge: the right answer
# is never a blend of two versions, it is a fresh scan of the merged tree.
#
# `merge=maz-inventory` names the driver that does exactly that. The driver's
# command lives in each checkout's own git config, not here — git will not take
# a command from a tracked file — so it is registered by
# tools/inventory/install-merge-driver.sh, which the session-start hook runs.
# Without that registration git falls back to an ordinary conflict, and the fix
# is one command: node tools/inventory/main.mjs --write
#
# linguist-generated keeps them collapsed in GitHub diffs, where a 600-line
# regenerated table is noise rather than review.
docs/INVENTORY.md    merge=maz-inventory linguist-generated=true
docs/inventory.json  merge=maz-inventory linguist-generated=true
